{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Send a kar.</b> A species of camel that runs, from the same root as הכרי והרצים (2 Kings 11:19). Some say it is \"the ruler of the land of stride,\" because its stride on the ground is larger than any other stride. The correct view is that כר is in construct state, for it is found only among rulers."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:53:57.361380003Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}